{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>How. Heilel.</b> What is close to understanding is that it is the planet Venus, and the witness is \"son of dawn,\" for it is seen near the degrees of dawn on certain days, and there is no star in all the host of heaven whose appearance is as luminous to the eye as it; therefore it is called heilel, from the root of לא יהלו אורם (Isaiah 13:10)." "<b>חולש.</b> Like ויחלש יהושע (Exodus 13:17). Some say: casting lots, in the sense of קלקל בחצים (Ezekiel 21:26)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {0 "Heilel left untranslated as it is the subject of Ibn Ezra's philological discussion; he derives it from the root ה-ל-ל.", 1 "The Exodus citation appears erroneous: ויחלש יהושע occurs at Exodus 17:13, not 13:17. Transmitted as found."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:53:46.524220478Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}